<div class="seg"><span class="seg-icon">🚗</span><div class="seg-txt"><strong>Richfield → Green River</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; ~120 mi &nbsp;·&nbsp; ~2 hrs &nbsp;·&nbsp; I-70 E · <strong>🏞️ This is a genuine scenic drive</strong> — I-70 cuts through the San Rafael Swell, a massive uplift of layered red rock that cars literally drive through. The highway was built through terrain that had no road at all until 1970. Watch for the Black Dragon Canyon pullout (mile marker 145) and the San Rafael Reef — a jagged wall of upturned sandstone fins. One of the most dramatic interstate stretches in the US.</div></div>

