<div class="seg"><span class="seg-icon">🚗</span><div class="seg-txt"><strong>Glenwood Springs → Silverthorne</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; ~90 mi &nbsp;·&nbsp; ~1.5 hrs &nbsp;·&nbsp; I-70 E · <strong>🏞️ Best mountain driving of the whole trip.</strong> Glenwood Canyon gives way to Dotsero → Eagle → Vail Valley. Vail itself is worth 10 minutes if you've never seen it — pull off at exit 176 just for the alpine village backdrop. Then Vail Pass (10,666 ft), Copper Mountain, and the Eisenhower Tunnel at 11,013 ft — the highest vehicular tunnel in the world. <strong>Scenic detour option:</strong> Just before the tunnel, take US-6 over Loveland Pass instead (adds 20 min) — a stunning open-air mountain road at 11,990 ft with 360° views and a famous Continental Divide sign. Dogs welcome at the summit pullout on leash.</div></div>

