<!-- TIPS -->
<div class="tips">
  <div class="tips-title">⚠️ Before You Go</div>
  <div class="tip"><strong>🐾 Weight limits:</strong> Most hotels cap at 40 lb. La Quinta properties have no weight limit and no pet fee — the best chain for large dogs. Always call ahead to confirm current policy; these change frequently.</div>
  <div class="tip"><strong>⚡ Trust the nav:</strong> Tesla's in-car routing accounts for real-time battery %, elevation, A/C load, and speed better than any static plan. Use these towns for flexibility — the app will tell you exactly where to stop.</div>
  <div class="tip"><strong>🏔️ Mountain passes:</strong> I-70 on the final day crosses Vail Pass and Eisenhower Tunnel (~11,013 ft). Check CDOT road conditions at cotrip.org before departing Glenwood Springs, especially in spring or fall.</div>
  <div class="tip"><strong>🌡️ Desert heat + dogs:</strong> The Barstow–Primm–Vegas–St. George corridor can hit 110°F+ in summer. Never leave the dog in the car (even briefly with the Tesla climate running — battery drain is real). Carry a collapsible water bowl and 2+ gallons of extra water. Do dog walks before 9am or after 5pm.</div>
  <div class="tip"><strong>⛽ Critical charge:</strong> Always top off fully at Grand Junction Mesa Mall OR Parachute before the canyon climb to Glenwood Springs. Elevation gain plus any A/C or heat load can consume significantly more battery than flat desert driving.</div>
  <div class="tip"><strong>🗺️ Flexibility is the point:</strong> This itinerary has more towns than you'll need — that's intentional. If you're running ahead of schedule, skip a stop; if behind, overnight somewhere new. Every town has what you need to be comfortable.</div>
